<title>FRANCE: Air France Jan-April 97 cargo tonnage share at ADP.</title>
<headline>Air France Jan-April 97 cargo tonnage share at ADP.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-06-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>Air France's share of global air cargo tonnage handled at the two Paris airports, Charles de Gaulle and Orly, in the first four months of 1997 was stable compared to 1996 as a whole, Aeroport de Paris (ADP) figures show.</p>
<p>Air France's share of ADP's global cargo tonnage in the period in question, totalling 365,702 tonnes, was 55.3 percent compared to 55.5 percent in 1996.</p>
<p>The top 10 cargo-handling airlines at the ADP, by tonnage share, in January-April 1997, together with 1996 full-year tonnage share, were:</p>
<p>		    Jan-April 1997	  1996</p>
<p>			    percent	  percent</p>
<p>  Air France	    55.3	     55.5</p>
<p>  Federal Express	7.5		6.8</p>
<p>  Air France Europe    2.8		3.8</p>
<p>(ex-Air Inter)</p>
<p>  American Airlines    2.2		2.0</p>
<p>  Air Canada	     2.1		1.7</p>
<p>  L'Aeropostale	  1.7		1.9</p>
<p>  Japan Airlines	 1.7		1.6</p>
<p>  United Airlines	1.6		1.3</p>
<p>  Air Outre Mer (AOM)  1.6	     n.a.</p>
<p>  Cathay Pacific	 1.6		1.8</p>
<p>- Reuters Air Cargo Newsroom Tel+44 171 542 7706 Fax+5017</p>
